Programme-Wide Learning Approach

All seven programmes should follow a practical, application-oriented learning model.

Learning components:

1. Structured concept-based learning
2. Demonstration of relevant AI tools
3. Guided practical exercises
4. Professional case studies and scenarios
5. Individual or group assignments
6. Capstone project
7. Final project review and feedback

Important Programme Notes

- Each course is an independent programme; learners may enrol according to their professional needs.
- Recommended duration is four weeks per course and should be confirmed against the final delivery schedule.
- Participants should have access to a computer and internet connection for hands-on activities.
- Free and paid AI tools may be demonstrated depending on availability. Tool subscriptions are not included unless explicitly stated.
- AI-generated outputs must be reviewed and verified by participants.
- Course completion does not imply professional certification, employment placement or guaranteed business results.
- Practical project work should be assessed against clearly defined learning criteria.

